---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Contribute to SimuBox">
  <div class="site-shell editorial-page">
    <div class="editorial-main">
      <p class="section-index">CONTRIBUTE / REVIEWED WORK</p>
      <h1>Make a model easier to study.</h1>
      <p class="editorial-lede">Contributions currently arrive through reviewed issues and pull requests. A clear scientific explanation is as valuable as an implementation.</p>
      <section><h2>Propose an experiment</h2><p>Describe the model, meaningful controls, assumptions and references. Include author attribution, source URL and license. Browser-compatible static output is the target; external code is not built or published automatically.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Improve an explanation</h2><p>Clarify the mathematics, numerical method or limitations in a scientific note. Cite claims. Keep manifest metadata in YAML so source, status and attribution have one authoritative record.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Review boundary</h2><p>External projects stay candidates until their source revision, license notices, dependencies, build artifact and isolated browser behavior are reviewed. Do not put secrets or executable build commands in manifests. See the <a href="https://github.com/selyaktini/simubox/blob/main/docs/SECURITY.md">security model</a>.</p></section>
    </div>
    <aside class="editorial-aside"><p class="section-index">SUBMISSION RECORD</p><h2>Include with a proposal</h2><ol><li>Scientific question and model.</li><li>Controls and expected observations.</li><li>Assumptions, limits and references.</li><li>Authors, repository and license.</li></ol><a href="https://github.com/selyaktini/simubox" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open the repository ↗</a></aside>
  </div>
</Base>
